  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1030 AM MDT Sun Jun 21 2026\n\nTHE REST OF TODAY: \n\nDaytime highs today will be running around normal, with generally \nsunny skies and lighter winds for the first day of Summer. \nGusty winds will mainly be confined to the Divide. Critical fire\nweather conditions exist today, but will be fairly localized. \nYou may be wondering why things are smoky/hazy today. This is \ndue to the Iron Fire which is burning in Salt Lake City's CWA. \nIt is currently mapped at just under 14,000 acres. The HRRR \nsmoke model shows that this smoke will stick with us through at\nleast tomorrow. \n\nSTART OF THE WORK WEEK & LATE WEEK MOISTURE CHANCES:\n\nThis week will be characterized by predominately zonal flow with a \nfew subtle shortwave troughs occasionally interrupting the flow. \nWith that being said, those subtle troughs will do little to break \nus out of the hot, dry, windy spell. Critical fire weather \nconditions will be around through at least mid-week, with southwest \nColorado getting in on the action first with gusts upwards of 30 \nmph. Red Flag Warnings (1PM-8PM) are in effect for most of southwest \nColorado for Monday. Expect gusty conditions to be around each \nafternoon for most of the CWA. See the Fire Weather section for more \ninformation on that. Temperatures are expected to peak Tuesday and \nWednesday, with triple digit highs forecasted for the desert valleys \nof eastern Utah and western Colorado. \n\nThere is finally some semblance of moisture returning to the \nregion later in the week. PWATs are forecasted to be around \n160-180% of normal, but it may be difficult for moisture to \nbreak through in the way of wetting rain due to the strong dry \nairmass we have been situated under for the past week or so. The\nGFS ensemble appears to keep moisture confined mainly to the \nFour Corners area, with the Euro Ensemble bringing chances for \nmoisture further north towards the I-70 corridor. Keep in mind, \nit is still fairly early to tell how this may pan out and HiRes \nguidance may begin to paint a better picture as the day gets \ncloser. Expect adjustments to the forecast as the week \nprogresses.",
